    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a roast dinner with pan gravy. Two thirds of that is the sausage, so a sale on brats moves this number more than anything else you can do.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSausage is two thirds of the cost.\u003c/strong\u003e Everything else on the list combined is a small fraction of the total. Buy brats on sale, freeze them, and this recipe gets meaningfully cheaper.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePotatoes and carrots are the cheap bulk.\u003c/strong\u003e Bagged potatoes and bagged carrots fill both pans for very little, and both keep for weeks.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eRed onions cost more than yellow.\u003c/strong\u003e They look prettier roasted, but if the board shows a gap, yellow onions do the identical job for less.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eThe gravy is butter, flour and broth.\u003c/strong\u003e That is a small line on the cost list and it beats any jarred gravy you can buy."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Heat the oven to 425F. Cut the potatoes into chunks, cut the carrots into thick batons, and cut the red onions into wedges.",
                    "Toss the vegetables with the olive oil, minced garlic, dried thyme, dried oregano, salt and black pepper, then spread them across two large sheet pans.",
                    "Nestle the bratwurst among the vegetables and roast until the sausages are browned and the vegetables are tender and caught at the edges.",
                    "Move the sausages and vegetables to a holding pan and keep them warm. Do not wash the roasting pan, because everything stuck to it is the gravy.",
                    "Set that pan across two burners, melt the butter in it, and scrape hard while it bubbles to lift all the browned bits.",
                    "Whisk in the flour and cook it for a minute, then pour in the beef broth in a steady stream while whisking until the gravy thickens.",
                    "Slice the sausages, combine them with the vegetables in your big pot, and pour the gravy over the top."
                ],
